# What you are writing: the chooser of what a document is, which is the
# template of its element, the Document type tab of Document properties.

chooser-title = What are you writing?
chooser-search = Search what can be written
chooser-search-placeholder = A kind of text, a journal, a publisher…
chooser-none-found = Nothing goes by that name.
# Where what the document is comes from an element over it: that element's name, and the name of what it is.
chooser-from = From { $name }: { $template }. What you choose here holds for this element and all under it.
chooser-again = Take it from { $name } again
# What a document is where nothing over it says otherwise: the writer's usual, by its name.
chooser-usual-again = Take { $name } again
# Under the one chosen: how its pages are set, and how it cites.
chooser-brings = Pages as { $layout }; citations in { $style }
chooser-brings-layout = Pages as { $layout }
chooser-usual-pages = your usual, { $name }
chooser-submission = Writing for a journal, a publisher or a style guide?
# The kind of text the list is narrowed to, by its name.
chooser-submission-narrowed = Those made for { $name }. Search to find the others.
chooser-submission-all = Each is made for a kind of text above, with what the journal, the publisher or the guide asks for.
chooser-own-from = Make a template of my own from this…
chooser-change-own = Change this template of mine…
chooser-of-project = Kept in the project: not among your own templates on this computer.
# In the menu of an element.
chooser-menu = Document type…
